course: dictionary
lesson: 695
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Many words have more than one meaning. The word bank is one of them. To know which meaning is right, read the words around it, because they are its context and they leave clues. «Toad, the greatest boaster on the river bank.» The word river tells you that bank means the land along the side of a river.
explain: «If a card is lost, the bank can freeze or block it at once.» Card and account are clues about money, so here bank means a place that keeps money safe and lends it. The same word can mean something quite different in another sentence, so always check the clues before you decide.
explain: Bank can also be a verb. To bank on something means to count on it. Try your meaning in the sentence instead of the hard word: if «I can bank on you» still makes sense with count on, you have the right meaning.
fact: A bank is a place that keeps money safe and lends it.
fact: A piggy bank is a small box for saving coins.
fact: The bank of a river is the land along its side.
fact: A bank can also be a store of things kept to use later, like a food bank or a blood bank.
fact: To bank on something means to count on it.
exercise: «Never jump in after a person or a dog: call, reach or throw from the bank.» Which meaning of bank fits here? | *The land along the side of a river | To count on something | A place that lends money | A box for saving coins
exercise: «If a card is lost, the bank can freeze or block it at once.» What does bank mean here? | The land along a river | A store of things kept to use later | To count on something | *A place that keeps money safe and lends it
exercise: «Clothes given to clothes banks are sorted: good ones are resold.» What does bank mean here? | To count on something | A box for saving coins | *A store of things kept to use later | The land beside a river
test: Ella says, «I can bank on Sam to help me.» What does bank on mean? | To sit beside a river | To lend coins to a friend | *To count on | To save money in
test: Mia puts her coins in her piggy bank. What is a piggy bank? | *A small box for saving coins | The land along a river | A store of blood for hospitals | A place that lends money
exam: Which meaning of bank fits «Toad, the greatest boaster on the river bank»? | To count on something | A store of things kept to use later | *The land along the side of a river | A place that keeps money safe
